// endpoint_watch_desktop_banners.proto — WatchDesktopBanners: the notifier
// app's one standing stream, over which the daemon hands it each desktop
// banner to post. DESKTOP NOTIFIER section.
//
// Zettel.app is the only caller. It is a resident background app (no window,
// no Dock icon) that posts every agent-repl desktop banner through macOS's
// notification center under its own name and icon. It opens this stream on
// the daemon `daemon.addr` advertises, and opens it again whenever a new
// daemon is advertised.
//
// ONE STREAM STANDS AT A TIME. A later stream SUPERSEDES an earlier one: the
// earlier is told `superseded` and ended, so two app instances never both
// post. While no stream stands, every banner the daemon wants is recorded as
// unposted, with the reason, and none is queued for later: a banner is about
// a moment, and a late one would steer the user to a stale workspace.

